{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00701",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.75,
      "end_seconds": 12.83,
      "duration_seconds": 12.08,
      "text": "Hi Mr Lowe, I'm Hannah, the nurse. Can I do your blood pressure and pulse while we wait for the doctor? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.99,
      "end_seconds": 23.16,
      "duration_seconds": 9.17,
      "text": "Yes, of course. Is that okay? I'm always nervous in here, my pressure goes through the roof. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 39.97,
      "end_seconds": 49.9,
      "duration_seconds": 9.93,
      "text": "Blood pressure 142 over 90, pulse 88. That's a touch up, but you're allowed to be nervous."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.74,
      "end_seconds": 63.1,
      "duration_seconds": 12.36,
      "text": "Hello, Mr Lowe. It's about six weeks since you started the physio and the heel pads. How are the heels?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.94,
      "end_seconds": 77.97,
      "duration_seconds": 14.03,
      "text": "A bit better, I think, but not right. I still get this pain at the back of both heels, especially first thing in the morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.0,
      "end_seconds": 84.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "How long does the morning pain last?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.35,
      "end_seconds": 97.76,
      "duration_seconds": 12.41,
      "text": "Half an hour, maybe an hour. And then it eases once I'm up and moving. I'm worried it's something nasty."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.25,
      "end_seconds": 105.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "Do you get back stiffness as well, in the morning?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.47,
      "end_seconds": 111.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "No, my back's fine. No stiffness at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.77,
      "end_seconds": 118.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "What are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.39,
      "end_seconds": 128.53,
      "duration_seconds": 7.14,
      "text": "Naproxen, 500 mg, twice a day, with food. It helps a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.46,
      "end_seconds": 133.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Remind me of your other conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.7,
      "end_seconds": 149.7,
      "duration_seconds": 13.0,
      "text": "Psoriasis, on my elbows, since my twenties. I had a red, sore eye once, iritis I think they said, two years ago. And acid reflux."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.43,
      "end_seconds": 162.82,
      "duration_seconds": 12.39,
      "text": "That history is useful, because those conditions can be linked. Let me see your heels. Can you lie on the couch? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.92,
      "end_seconds": 169.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.73,
      "text": "Yes, sorry, my feet are a bit cold. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 190.49,
      "end_seconds": 194.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "I'll put a blanket over you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.45,
      "end_seconds": 210.69,
      "duration_seconds": 14.24,
      "text": "Tender at the back of both heels, right where the Achilles tendon attaches to the bone, and there's no swelling or redness of the tendons."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.96,
      "end_seconds": 218.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.88,
      "text": "Is it a tear? I read about Achilles tears. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.66,
      "end_seconds": 232.58,
      "duration_seconds": 10.92,
      "text": "No, a tear would feel different, with a sudden pain and weakness. This is irritation where the tendon meets the bone. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.15,
      "end_seconds": 237.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "So what's causing it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.45,
      "end_seconds": 253.95,
      "duration_seconds": 15.5,
      "text": "Psoriasis, a past inflamed eye, and morning heel pain at the tendon attachments make me think I can't rule out an inflammatory arthritis linked to psoriasis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.43,
      "end_seconds": 259.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Arthritis? At forty-four? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.05,
      "end_seconds": 275.4,
      "duration_seconds": 13.35,
      "text": "It can happen at any age, and it's treatable. I don't want to jump to conclusions, which is why we'll look more carefully. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.18,
      "end_seconds": 281.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Will it get worse? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.39,
      "end_seconds": 292.64,
      "duration_seconds": 9.25,
      "text": "If it is inflammatory, treating it early protects the joints. That's the reason to find out. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 295.39,
      "end_seconds": 300.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "Doctor, shall I book him with the rheumatologist? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.74,
      "end_seconds": 315.25,
      "duration_seconds": 13.51,
      "text": "Yes please, Hannah. I'd like you to see a specialist, Mr Lowe, and I'd like to see you in six weeks as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.75,
      "end_seconds": 319.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Six weeks. Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.2,
      "end_seconds": 327.81,
      "duration_seconds": 6.61,
      "text": "Keep up with the stretches and the heel pads, and avoid hard flat shoes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 329.53,
      "end_seconds": 335.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "I will. Thank you, doctor. You've calmed me down. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 336.12,
      "end_seconds": 340.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "See you in six weeks, Mr Lowe. ~"
    }
  ]
}
